            <ArticleTitle>Gout: nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs and colchicine to prevent painful flares during early urate-lowering therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>397-401</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3109/15360288.2010.526689</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case report on a gout patient is presented with discussion of the use of prophylactic agents for prevention of gouty flare in such a patient when beginning urate-lowering therapy. The limitations of the literature on this subject are described. Advantages and disadvantages of of prophylaxis and the burden of pain are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
